{{!-- One menu item with a submenu, in the bar or the overlay.

Called by chrome/nav-tree.hbs with the parent item as its context, plus `variant` and `items` (the
whole menu, from which the children are collected by their "Parent / " prefix). Inside the
children loop `../label` is the parent's label: the loop's items are other objects, so the frame
is always pushed.

THE BAR is the reference build's NavDropdown, ported: the panel opens on hover AND on keyboard
focus, so a pointer and a keyboard reach the same places; Escape closes it and puts focus back on
the label (the reference build closed the panel around the focused item, which dropped focus to
<body>; focusing the label first re-opens it through `focusin`, so the close comes second); focus
leaving the group closes it (`relatedTarget` is checked, so moving between the label and its own
panel does not); one panel is open at a time, with a 200ms grace period on close so a diagonal move
from the label down to a lower item does not lose it. All of that state is the `nav` store in
assets/js/main.js. The label still navigates, unless its URL is `#` — a parent that is only a
heading, like the demo's Others — which renders as a button instead, and a click on that button
opens the panel: that is how a keyboard brings it back after Escape. It opens rather than toggles,
because a pointer has already opened it on the way in. The panel's box starts flush under the
label and its visible 8px offset is its own transparent padding, so there is no dead zone to cross
on the way down.

The parent reads as current when it or any child is: `:has([aria-current=page])` on the group, so
the marker is decided by the same flags Ghost computed for each item and nothing is compared twice.

THE OVERLAY draws a group as a heading with its children listed under it, the reference build's
mobile menu, because a panel that opens inside a full-screen panel is a second navigation problem.
The heading is a link when the parent has a URL of its own, so a parent page stays reachable below
the breakpoint too. Space opens above every group but the first, and below one that a plain item
follows — without it a top-level link reads as the last child of the group above it. --}}
{{#match variant "bar"}}
	<div
		class="group/nav relative"
		x-on:mouseenter="$store.nav.show('{{slug}}')"
		x-on:mouseleave="$store.nav.hide()"
		x-on:focusin="$store.nav.show('{{slug}}')"
		x-on:focusout="if (!$el.contains($event.relatedTarget)) $store.nav.hideNow()"
		x-on:keydown.escape="$el.firstElementChild.focus(); $store.nav.hideNow()">
		<{{#match url "~$" "#"}}button{{else}}a{{/match}}
			{{#match url "~$" "#"}}type="button" x-on:click="$store.nav.show('{{slug}}')"{{else}}href="{{url}}"{{/match}}
			{{#if current}}aria-current="page"{{/if}}
			aria-haspopup="true"
			aria-expanded="false"
			aria-controls="nav-menu-{{slug}}"
			x-bind:aria-expanded="($store.nav.open === '{{slug}}').toString()"
			class="font-ui text-muted hover:text-text group-has-[[aria-current=page]]/nav:text-text group-has-[[aria-current=page]]/nav:after:bg-accent relative flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-1 border-0 bg-transparent p-0 text-[15px] no-underline after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:-bottom-[5px] after:h-[2px]">{{> "chrome/nav-label" iconSize="h-[15px]"}}<span
				aria-hidden="true"
				class="text-[9px] leading-none opacity-70">▾</span></{{#match url "~$" "#"}}button{{else}}a{{/match}}>

		<div
			x-show="$store.nav.open === '{{slug}}'"
			x-cloak
			class="absolute top-full left-0 z-40 pt-2">
			<div
				id="nav-menu-{{slug}}"
				class="border-border bg-surface min-w-[15rem] rounded-md border py-2 shadow-md">
				<ul class="flex list-none flex-col">
					{{#foreach items}}
						{{#match label "~^" (concat ../label " / ")}}
							<li>
								<a
									href="{{url}}"
									{{#if current}}aria-current="page"{{/if}}
									class="font-ui hover:bg-surface-2 block px-4 py-2 text-sm whitespace-nowrap no-underline {{#if current}}text-accent font-semibold{{else}}text-text{{/if}}">{{> "chrome/nav-child-label"}}</a>
							</li>
						{{/match}}
					{{/foreach}}
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
{{/match}}

{{#match variant "overlay"}}
	<div class="not-first:pt-5 [&:has(+a)]:pb-5">
		{{#match url "~$" "#"}}
			<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted uppercase">{{label}}</p>
		{{else}}
			<a
				href="{{url}}"
				{{#if current}}aria-current="page"{{/if}}
				x-on:click="close()"
				class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta hover:text-accent uppercase no-underline {{#if current}}text-accent{{else}}text-muted{{/if}}">{{label}}</a>
		{{/match}}
		<div class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2.5">
			{{#foreach items}}
				{{#match label "~^" (concat ../label " / ")}}
					<a
						href="{{url}}"
						{{#if current}}aria-current="page"{{/if}}
						x-on:click="close()"
						class="font-ui text-[17px] no-underline {{#if current}}text-accent{{else}}text-text hover:text-accent{{/if}}">{{> "chrome/nav-child-label"}}</a>
				{{/match}}
			{{/foreach}}
		</div>
	</div>
{{/match}}
